// @error: null is not callable
// `list.next` is not part of the language. gopherbuzz used to expose it as an
// explicit iterator protocol; upstream removed it from the user surface (the same
// change that stopped exposing map.next), so keeping it meant accepting a program
// upstream rejects - the permissiveness direction that matters most. Nothing in
// this workspace or upstream's own tests used it.
//
// The rejection is a runtime "null is not callable" rather than upstream's
// compile-time [E57] "List property doesn't exist", because that is how every
// unknown list member behaves here. Both refuse the program.
final xs = [1, 2, 3];
final __r = xs.next(0);
